---
import FutureTechMissionFrame from '../../../../components/FutureTechMissionFrame.astro';
---
<FutureTechMissionFrame
  missionNumber="1"
  title="Make It Happen"
  tagline="Code your first micro:bit and make it respond to you."
  question="How can I give a tiny computer instructions and make it respond to me?"
  success="I can create code, run it on a micro:bit, make it respond to an input, and explain what my code is doing."
  nextTitle="Mission 2 — Make It Think"
  nextHref="../mission-2-make-it-think/"
>
  <section id="stage-1" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">01</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">GET READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Set Up</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Grab your tools, find the four parts you will use today, and make sure your station is ready.</p><div class="check-list"><span>☐ Computer</span><span>☐ micro:bit</span><span>☐ USB data cable</span><span>☐ Mission page open</span></div><p class="concept">Find these four parts: Button A · Button B · 5×5 LED display · USB port.</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Button A + Button B</strong><p>These are <b>inputs</b>. You press them to give information to the program.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>LED display</strong><p>This is an <b>output</b>. Your program can make it show images, numbers, and words.</p></article></div><p class="mini-label">If you are working with a partner</p><div class="partner-strip"><span><strong>DRIVER</strong><small>Controls the computer and connects the micro:bit.</small></span><span><strong>NAVIGATOR</strong><small>Reads the next step, predicts results, and checks requirements.</small></span></div><p class="success">Start with these roles. Switch at Stage 3. Both partners must be able to explain the code.</p><p class="mini-label">Maker rules</p><div class="check-list"><span>☐ Handle equipment carefully</span><span>☐ Keep food and drinks away</span><span>☐ Never force a connection</span><span>☐ Return everything when finished</span></div></section>
  <section id="stage-2" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">02</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">FIRST SUCCESS</p><h2 class="stage-title">First Code</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Create a tiny program, test it on screen, then send it to the real micro:bit.</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>1 — Open MakeCode</strong><p>Open <a class="external" href="https://makecode.microbit.org/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">MakeCode for micro:bit ↗</a>. Choose <b>New Project</b>. Name it <code>FirstName_L1_M1</code>.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>2 — Make your first program</strong><p>Put <code>show string</code> inside <code>on start</code>. Type your initials.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>3 — Test the simulator</strong><p>Your initials should scroll across the virtual micro:bit on screen.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>4 — Run it for real</strong><p>Connect the micro:bit with USB. Click <b>Download</b> and send the newest program to the device.</p></article></div>
    <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Visual MakeCode model for first code"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL</span><strong>Compare your workspace to this</strong></div><div class="block-finder"><span><b>Basic</b> → show string</span><span><b>On start</b> is already on the workspace</span></div><div class="code-columns one"><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block event">on start</div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show string <span class="value">“AJ”</span></div></div></div><p class="code-model-note">Your initials can be different. The important part is that <b>show string</b> is inside <b>on start</b>.</p></aside>
    <p class="success">✓ Success looks like this: your initials scroll across the real micro:bit.</p><p class="warning">If it does not work: compare your blocks to the model, test the simulator, check the cable, then download the newest version again.</p><p class="concept">Mini Check: point to the <b>output</b>. The LED display is the output because it shows the result of the program.</p></section>
  <section id="stage-3" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">03</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">INPUT → CODE → OUTPUT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Make It React</h2></div></div><p class="success"><b>WORKING WITH A PARTNER? SWITCH ROLES NOW.</b></p><div class="route"><span>INPUT: Button</span><span>CODE: Event</span><span>OUTPUT: LED display</span></div><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge A — Button A</strong><p>Add <code>on button A pressed</code>. Put <code>show icon</code> inside it. Pick any icon.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge B — Button B</strong><p>Add <code>on button B pressed</code>. Make it show something different.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Challenge C — Sequence</strong><p>Make one button run at least three instructions. Example: image → pause → image.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>What is a sequence?</strong><p>A <b>sequence</b> is a set of instructions happening in order.</p></article></div>
    <aside class="code-model" aria-label="Visual MakeCode model for button events and sequence"><div class="code-model-head"><span>CODE MODEL</span><strong>Your blocks can look like this</strong></div><div class="block-finder"><span><b>Input</b> → on button pressed</span><span><b>Basic</b> → show icon</span><span><b>Basic</b> → pause</span><span><b>Basic</b> → show string</span></div><div class="code-columns"><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block input">on button <span class="value">A</span> pressed</div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show icon <span class="value">♥</span></div><div class="mk-block basic indent">pause <span class="value">500 ms</span></div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show icon <span class="value">☺</span></div></div><div class="code-stack"><div class="mk-block input">on button <span class="value">B</span> pressed</div><div class="mk-block basic indent">show string <span class="value">“AJ”</span></div></div></div><p class="code-model-note">This is one example, not an answer you must copy. Your two buttons should do different things, and one event needs a three-step sequence.</p></aside>
    <p class="success">✓ Before moving on: test A, test B, and run the program on the physical micro:bit.</p><p class="warning">If an animation changes too fast, add a pause between images. If something does not run, use TRY 4 and compare the order of your blocks to the model.</p></section>
  <section id="stage-4" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">04</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">YOUR CREATION</p><h2 class="stage-title">Build It — Interactive Badge</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Create a digital badge that tells us something about you. It must react differently to Button A and Button B.</p><div class="check-list"><span>☐ Button A works</span><span>☐ Button B works</span><span>☐ The responses are different</span><span>☐ One response uses a sequence</span><span>☐ It runs on the real micro:bit</span><span>☐ You changed it to make it yours</span></div><p class="mini-label">Need an idea?</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Idea 1</strong><p>A = favourite activity · B = initials + animation.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Idea 2</strong><p>A = happy face · B = favourite number.</p></article></div><div class="try4"><strong>STUCK? TRY 4</strong><p>1. CHECK — compare your blocks to the code model. 2. SIMULATE the newest code. 3. DOWNLOAD the newest version. 4. PARTNER — explain what should happen. Still stuck? Ask for help and say what you already tried.</p></div></section>
  <section id="stage-5" class="stage"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">05</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">OPTIONAL CHALLENGE</p><h2 class="stage-title">Level It Up</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Only after Build It works. Choose one while you wait for your checkpoint.</p><div class="level-grid"><article class="level-card"><strong>Shake It</strong><p>Make shaking the micro:bit trigger an output.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>A + B</strong><p>Add a third response when A and B are pressed together.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Animator</strong><p>Create an animation with at least five frames.</p></article><article class="level-card"><strong>Explorer</strong><p>Find another MakeCode input and make it work.</p></article></div><p class="success">When every Build It box is checked, add your name or pair to the Ready-for-Check queue. Keep Leveling Up until you are called.</p></section>
  <section id="stage-6" class="stage checkpoint"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">06</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SHOW WHAT YOU KNOW</p><h2 class="stage-title">Checkpoint</h2></div></div><p class="intro">Bring your micro:bit and open your code when you are called. Each student completes the checkpoint individually.</p><div class="step-grid"><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 1 — Make It Work</strong><p>Press A or B. Identify the <b>input</b> and the <b>output</b>.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 2 — Explain It</strong><p>Point to one event. Explain what makes that code run.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>Check 3 — Change It</strong><p>Make one small change chosen by the teacher. Test the new version.</p></article><article class="step-card"><strong>After Your Check</strong><p><b>PASS</b> = Mission Complete. <b>NOT YET</b> = fix one skill and retry.</p></article></div></section>
  <section class="stage passport"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">✓</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">SKILL PASSPORT</p><h2 class="stage-title">Mission 1 Skills</h2></div></div><div class="check-list"><span>☐ I can run code on a micro:bit</span><span>☐ I can use an input</span><span>☐ I can create an output</span><span>☐ I can use an event and sequence</span><span>☐ I can change and test my code</span></div></section>
  <section class="stage reset"><div class="stage-head"><span class="stage-number">↺</span><div><p class="stage-kicker">LEAVE IT READY</p><h2 class="stage-title">Reset</h2></div></div><div class="check-list"><span>☐ Project saved correctly</span><span>☐ micro:bit back in the numbered kit</span><span>☐ USB cable loosely coiled</span><span>☐ Kit complete and workspace clear</span><span>☐ Damage or missing equipment reported</span></div><p class="concept">Exit question: What is one thing you made the micro:bit do today?</p></section>
</FutureTechMissionFrame>
<style is:global>
.code-model{margin:.8rem 0;padding:.9rem;border:1px solid #c7d2fe;border-radius:15px;background:linear-gradient(135deg,#f8faff,#f5f3ff)}.code-model-head{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:.75rem;align-items:center;margin-bottom:.55rem}.code-model-head span{color:#6d28d9;font:900 .66rem ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;letter-spacing:.09em}.code-model-head strong{color:#26324a;font-size:.9rem}.block-finder{display:flex;gap:.4rem;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:.7rem}.block-finder span{padding:.34rem .5rem;border:1px solid #dbe3ef;border-radius:999px;background:#fff;color:#52617a;font-size:.72rem;font-weight:750}.block-finder b{color:#5b21b6}.code-columns{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.7rem;align-items:start}.code-columns.one{grid-template-columns:minmax(0,520px)}.code-stack{display:grid;gap:.28rem;padding:.65rem;border-radius:12px;background:#111827}.mk-block{width:max-content;max-width:100%;padding:.48rem .62rem;border-radius:7px;color:#fff;font:800 .78rem/1.25 ui-monospace,SFMono-Regular,Menlo,monospace;box-shadow:inset 0 -2px rgba(0,0,0,.16)}.mk-block.event{background:#7c3aed}.mk-block.input{background:#c026d3}.mk-block.basic{background:#2563eb}.mk-block.indent{margin-left:1rem}.mk-block .value{display:inline-block;margin-left:.18rem;padding:.05rem .3rem;border-radius:4px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.2)}.code-model-note{margin:.6rem 0 0;color:#59677c;font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.45}.code-model-note b{color:#37205f}@media(max-width:680px){.code-model-head{display:grid}.code-columns,.code-columns.one{grid-template-columns:1fr}.mk-block{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box}.mk-block.indent{width:calc(100% - .75rem);margin-left:.75rem}}
</style>
